WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.580
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.450
At the last match, you guys gained a new weapon.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.160
Instead of thinking of
this skill as your final goal,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:25.500
think of it as a starting point to develop
even larger movements to compete with.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.080
But if you sacrifice team cohesion for it,
you might as well forget it.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.330
Wing and guards, widen your fields of view.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.660
Be mindful of the triangular formation
and adjust your positions.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.330
You're aiming for synchronization and unison.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.830
You should strive to have a fusion
of unexpected dynamic movements

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:45.200
and a precisely calculated routine.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.160
Frankly, St. Clavis and Chutei University High
have higher individual skill.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.200
But the skill of each team
as a whole is a different story.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.540
All right, let's start practice.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:57.580
Yes, sir!

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.450
"Episode 9
One Lead"

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.330
Aiming to perfect the respective styles
the coach suggested to us,

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.290
we began to practice.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:43.450
Naturally, it wasn't all smooth sailing,
and we didn't always see eye to eye.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:46.410
But it was all for the goal
of refining the routine,

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:50.580
"7th Competition"

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:50.580
and I think we all felt that we were
improving greatly day by day.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:55.870
Then, we skated in the
seventh competition of the series,

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.790
which was our third and last preliminary match...

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.500
"Free Skate
Ionodai High School"

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.250
...and placed first for both the
short program and free skate.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.250
"Congratulations
Qualifying for Grand Prix Finals"

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.250
Naturally, we got the top score
for the seventh competition.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.200
"1st: St. Clavis Gakuin High School
2nd: Chutei University Kamimaezu High School
3rd: Eimei Academy High School
4th: Ionodai High School"

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.160
Fourth in the overall standings!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.120
We've pretty much secured a spot
at the Grand Prix finals.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.870
--Yeah!
--All right!

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.750
The fourth competition against
Shinozaki's team did it for us.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.830
That score would've been
at the top in any other match.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.950
It made up for our loss
at the first competition.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.410
Don't sulk.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.120
I'm not sulking!

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.370
As expected, Taiga's team is in first, huh?

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.410
They do have Shinozaki, too...

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.620
In second is Chutei University Kamimaezu
High School with the Ishikawa brothers?

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:38.620
No surprise there.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:39.910
Who's in third and fifth?

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:43.330
Hokkaido's Eimei Academy
and Ehime's Matsuyama Fukuonji.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:48.120
"3rd: Eimei Academy High School
4th: Ionodai High School"

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:48.120
Both are first timers to the finals,
and it's the first school from Ehime ever.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.790
"3rd: Eimei Academy High School
4th: Ionodai High School"

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.790
The top five teams are
pretty much set for the finals.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.870
"3rd: Eimei Academy High School
4th: Ionodai High School"

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.870
Really?

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.540
"3rd: Eimei Academy High School
4th: Ionodai High School"

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.540
There's a wide point gap
between fifth and sixth.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.790
In the eighth and last
competition of the series,

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:01.120
there aren't any schools that
can clear that gap to snatch fifth.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.120
But they have a chance at sixth?

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:06.250
The only teams left who stand a chance
are Himekawa's and Kuonji's teams.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:10.250
"Kogahara"

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:10.250
The only teams left who stand a chance
are Himekawa's and Kuonji's teams.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.500
"Person of the Week
Mi*Leon Noa"

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.500
You're amazing, Kuonji. Didn't you
just establish the club this year?

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:15.290
You're amazing, Kuonji. Didn't you
just establish the club this year?

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.700
You're too kind. It's thanks to their hard work.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.830
You've come this far. You'll be aiming
to qualify for the Grand Prix finals

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.040
with top scores in the eighth competition?

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.040
In order to live up to your expectations...

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.040
...we'll do our best!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.660
We'll be rooting for you. Let's hear it...

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:37.000
--Mi*Leon!
--Noa!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.910
I hope you'll all cheer them on, too!

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.040
Please do!

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.040
"Congratulations
Qualifying for Grand Prix Finals"

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.040
What?!

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.790
Hey. Hello, there.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:48.950
Number Two Prince...

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.000
What are you doing here?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.700
You were just on TV...

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.660
I'm heading home from recording.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.080
Can I have a minute?

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.160
What'd you bring me all the way out here for?

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.290
Sorry!

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.540
I came today to apologize.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:12.450
Do you remember how I invited
you to join my team before?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:16.080
Yeah... I turned you down, though.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.450
I'd like to retract that offer.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.830
I turned you down already!

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:23.660
All my teammates were complete amateurs.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.160
In addition to their idol activities,
they worked hard for the team

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.790
during spare moments of their busy schedules.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:36.620
It's partly thanks to their efforts
that the Grand Prix finals is within reach.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.540
It's mostly thanks to me, though.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:40.830
Hey.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:44.750
But I'm not lying about their effort.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:49.250
They resolved to follow me
despite their various circumstances,

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:51.290
and I cannot betray them.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.950
So, I'm sorry. Please let me retract my offer!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.160
No, I'm--

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:59.750
In exchange, I'll build a team
to invite all of you guys to join!

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.160
It's a promise!

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.080
You really don't--

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.080
I'm so glad. I knew you would consent.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.410
Listen when I'm talking!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:09.370
Oh, sorry, I have to go
to my next appointment.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:10.200
See you.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.500
Hey, wait!

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.500
Oh, yes. I almost forgot.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.950
<i>My</i> team will be the champions
of the Grand Prix finals.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.790
Ah, hello? Is my manager there?

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.200
About my interview tonight... so right!

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.080
"Congratulations
Qualifying for Grand Prix Finals"

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.870
"Congratulations
Qualifying for Grand Prix Finals"

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.870
What do I think of Noa Kuonji?

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:33.580
Yeah. You competed against him before,
so I thought you'd know something.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.120
Well?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.250
Look, he was in Montreal and Vancouver
and such when we were juniors.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.450
Oh, maple syrup...

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.080
You forgot about him?

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.370
A loud nuisance.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.620
Nothing about him as a competitor?

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.160
What about you, Kurayoshi?

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.750
With that personality, he's always positive
and isn't afraid to make mistakes.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.700
I had the impression that he liked
using a lot of daring elements.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.830
But back then, he didn't
have the build for it yet.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.250
He made a lot of mistakes.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.080
Does he have the build for it now?

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.370
I don't know.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:07.790
But he might have an ideal proportion
of body weight versus muscle mass now.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:12.700
The talk's all about Kuonji, but we
should be careful of Himekawa, too.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:18.160
Of course. Terauchi's team lost a lot
of skill when Himekawa left.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.290
I've known him since I was a kid,

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.450
but he's the opposite of Kuonji
and is super consistent.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.660
And at a really high level, too.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:30.200
Even though he's not the talkative type,

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.450
he's got a fiery competitive
spirit burning within.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:41.830
Are you okay?

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.700
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.330
Sorry, I'll keep up next time.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:47.750
Thanks.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.580
That's enough. Twenty-minute break.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.080
I heard you stayed late practicing
on your own last night, too.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.790
I appreciate your enthusiasm,
but it's not good to overdo it.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:06.950
Before a competition--

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:10.790
I know. I won't push myself
and will rest my body.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.830
But I'm this team's ace.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:18.910
With one lead, the ace's performance
has a greater impact on the scores.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.330
I won't let this end
without going to the finals.

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:31.660
One, two, three, four...

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:32.870
One...

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.410
You're still at it?

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.910
Manager.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:41.330
How many hours have you been here?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.040
No worries. I've still got changes of clothes.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.200
Where are Hanano and the others?

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.540
I sent them home. They had a shoot
hiking a mountain from the morning.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.330
I wanted to be on the safe side.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:52.250
Sounds rough.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.750
Please finish up soon.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.450
Gotcha, thanks.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:00.910
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.290
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.290
Kiriyama, Yuki, and I are going to
watch the eighth competition today.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.160
It's not far from here.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:10.200
I'll be going, too, to scout out the enemy.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.540
What will the rest of you do?

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:13.040
I'm going to practice.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.370
Same here. I've got some iffy spots still.

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:18.830
I'm staying. I promised Jonouchi
to be his practice partner.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:21.160
Of course I'm going to be practicing, too.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:26.790
What?! Don't ask me if I don't have a choice!

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:30.080
We're at the final stage!

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.790
With the chance to skate in the
Grand Prix finals on the line,

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.080
it's the eighth and final competition

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.500
of the Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix!

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.500
Laughing or crying,
this will decide the six teams

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:43.040
that will compete in the Grand Prix finals!

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:45.750
But we have a rare encounter
of two top-class schools.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:46.700
That's right.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:51.500
"Izumi Himekawa" "Noa Kuonji"
"Boys' High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix"

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:51.500
Against Kogahara High School,
whose routine supports their ace, Himekawa,

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.910
"Izumi Himekawa" "Noa Kuonji"
"Boys' High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix"

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.910
is Yokohama Super Global High School,

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:58.040
"Izumi Himekawa" "Noa Kuonji"
"Boys' High School Skate-Leading Grand Prix"

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:58.040
in a routine where their ace, Kuonji,
backs up his teammates.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.790
The fateful eighth competition
will start shortly!

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.000
"Athlete Waiting Rooms"

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.500
Did you come to cheer me on, Maeshima?!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.160
What? No.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.250
Oh, I'm so grateful.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.250
I said I'm not!

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.620
I'll be cheering for you! Please do your best!

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:21.660
I bought your new song,
“Love Passion on the Rink☆”!

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.540
Oh, thank you so much!

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:24.660
We'll do our best!

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.660
Please watch...

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:26.660
...our...

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.910
...shining performance of dreams!

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:30.500
Yes, I will.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.750
Himekawa.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:35.580
Mr. Kumada, thank you
for your help the other day.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.620
There's no need for that. Go on, Izumi.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.250
It's been a while.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:45.080
I've seen you in the competitions,
though, so it doesn't seem like it.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.000
Hey.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:50.160
Losing you really was a heavy blow to our team.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:54.120
I didn't have any problems
with the team or anything. I just--

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.450
No need to explain.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:59.870
It seems you'll be able to keep
the promise we made.

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:01.500
Let's meet next at nationals.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.200
We'll be waiting for you at the finals.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.000
I'll be there soon.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:12.830
Well, don't count your chickens
before they hatch, huh?

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:16.120
I know you guys are strong, Himekawa.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.830
But the ones to win and get
to the Grand Prix finals...

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:21.080
...will be us.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.580
I know you guys are strong, too.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.700
But the ones to earn our ticket
to the finals will be us.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:30.950
Yeah. Let's both give it our all.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:31.950
Yeah.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.370
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:44.120
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:44.120
We're halfway through the eighth
competition of the Grand Prix Series.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.830
All six teams have finished
their short programs,

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.700
and we are now at the intermission.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.370
You're watching, after all?

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:54.250
Aren't we on break? I'm just killing time.

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:59.290
Let's review the current standings.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:02.950
In first after the short program
is Niigata's Kogahara High School.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.700
They've made huge progress, getting this far.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:09.200
And their teamwork has grown quite strong.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:13.790
In a close second is Kanagawa's
Yokohama Super Global High School.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.910
Even in team skating,
Kuonji is still very strong!

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:20.540
His teammates are very expressive
and not to be taken lightly.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:24.830
Behind them with a somewhat larger point gap

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:29.370
are Fukushima's Kusano Mukaibara
and Wakayama's Tanabe Ryujin.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.200
What are your thoughts, Ms. Abe?
Who will you be looking out for?

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:35.540
I'll definitely be looking out
for Kogahara High School

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:38.870
and Yokohama Super Global High School,
who are vying for a spot at the finals,

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:39.950
but I hope to see the other teams
giving a good fight

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.000
"Fly, Aki Shoshikan High School"

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.000
but I hope to see the other teams
giving a good fight

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.660
"Fly, Aki Shoshikan High School"

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.660
to achieve the highest overall scores they can.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:44.950
"Fly, Aki Shoshikan High School"

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:44.950
Yes.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.040
Now, the momentous
free skate is about to begin.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.540
First to skate in the first half
is Hiroshima's Aki Shoshikan High School.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.410
"Hiroshima
Aki Shoshikan High School"

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.410
First to skate in the first half
is Hiroshima's Aki Shoshikan High School.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:58.830
"Hiroshima
Aki Shoshikan High School"

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.370
What the heck is all that?

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:07.950
Can't you tell? It's limited-edition merch
from this venue. Limited edition!

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:10.410
Not gonna give you any even if you ask.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:14.000
Are you a small child?
Be careful not to talk to strangers.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:17.330
How do you think this will turn out, Kiriyama?

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:20.660
Even without bias for Himekawa
because he's our former teammate,

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.120
I think that his team has the advantage.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:25.830
They're not widely known, but there's
a difference in experience level.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:29.330
They've also had the same coach
since they were juniors,

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.450
so they have strong team cohesion.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:36.000
But Yokohama Super Global
High School has Kuonji.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.290
He was said to be Shinozaki's rival.

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.500
I'm the one who'll beat Shinozaki.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.830
Yeah, yeah. We know already. Stay. Stay.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.540
You've said that before.
What's “stay” mean anyway?

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:51.750
Keep your calm. Um, it means you're
cooler when you remain calm.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:53.080
Oh?

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:57.950
Going back to what we were saying,
Kuonji's teammates' skill level is unknown.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.160
They give off the impression
that they're entertainers--

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.750
You don't believe in Rui's team?! I'm shocked!

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:03.080
No, that's not what I meant--

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.410
Do you even know how hard they've worked? Hm?!

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.580
Um, sorry--

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.750
I'm not trying to get you to apologize!

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:11.950
Unknown doesn't necessarily mean unskilled.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.080
Yes! Yes, that's right!

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.910
Preparation for the second half
of the free skate will begin shortly.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:23.660
This concludes the six-minute warmup.
Please leave the ice.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:25.040
Repeat...

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:28.000
Guys, you've done well
sticking with me up until now.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:31.750
Our final performance
for this series is about to start.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:37.120
I'm sure you've gotten angry at or
wanted to abandon my crazy demands.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:41.080
But you've come this far
in such a short period of time.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.620
That in itself is something to be proud of.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:47.120
I take pride in this team.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:53.120
But since we're here, let's give the best
performance and get the utmost glory.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.410
Together, the five of us!

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.790
--Yes!
--Let's compete in the Grand Prix finals...

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:57.910
And win it!

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.410
Let's do this, Captain!

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.290
Yeah.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.250
Here we go.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.250
Yeah!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.950
Yokohama Super Global High School!

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:11.870
--Mi*Leon!
--Noa!

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.790
Are they done?

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:19.790
There's nothing more I have to say
to you all. Fight with all you've got.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.200
Yes, sir!

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:26.830
This might not be the right time
to say this, but thanks, Himekawa.

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:29.700
It's thanks to you that
we were able to come this far.

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:34.750
You did your best on your own, and we
desperately practiced to keep up with you.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.830
Thanks to that, you raised
the standard of the whole team.

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.870
It's a dream to have a chance
of going to finals.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.160
I'm very grateful.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.040
It was brutal, though.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.830
You can say that again.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:52.450
Um, same here. I came suddenly,
but you accepted me and made me the ace.

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:56.120
Of course. We want to win, too!

00:15:56.120 --> 00:16:00.080
All right, let's give this everything
we've got, leaving no regrets.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.040
Yeah!

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:04.370
It's fine if you have regrets.

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:08.790
I don't intend for this to be our last.

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:11.750
"Free Skate
Kusano Mukaibara High School"

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.120
They've done it!

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:16.830
First to skate in the second half,
Fukushima's Kusano Mukaibara High School

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.500
"1. Kusano Mukaibara High School
2. Tanabe Ryujin High School"

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.500
First to skate in the second half,
Fukushima's Kusano Mukaibara High School

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.040
"1. Kusano Mukaibara High School
2. Tanabe Ryujin High School"

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.040
has received their best ever
score and stands in first!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:21.910
That was a great performance.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:25.500
Yes, breaking their personal best
should give them a confidence boost.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.620
We can expect tremendous growth
from them next year.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:31.700
Second to skate in the second half
is a team aiming for the Grand Prix finals,

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.660
the noteworthy Yokohama
Super Global High School.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:37.790
What kind of performance will they give?

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:39.790
It seems that Yokohama Super Global High School

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:43.330
has altered their free skate routine for
today's eighth competition of the series.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.540
What?!

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.870
There's no rule against it,

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:49.830
but considering the amount of practice
and refinement necessary for a routine,

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:53.540
it's typical to skate the same
program throughout a series.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.620
Yeah, this is suicide.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.290
"Yokohama Super Global High School"

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:01.410
Conversely, it might just show
how much confidence they have.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.750
Confidence?

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.410
What is this?

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:22.120
Are they trying to specialize
in entertainment shows?

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.120
Is this allowed?

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:36.790
Guess so. They're still skating.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:40.040
He's taken us all by surprise.

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:11.250
The skaters are encouraging
the audience to clap along.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.450
We've never seen anything like this before.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:26.950
Ms. Abe, is this still considered skate-leading?

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:30.000
They're still executing the required elements.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.620
Could this be a new possibility
for skate-leading?

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:56.870
Since when did figure skating
become such an aloof sport?

00:18:56.870 --> 00:19:01.330
I want more people to watch figure skating!

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:06.750
So I will aim to win with fun figure skating!

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:08.910
That's our style!

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:34.950
You guys were amazing! Rui, Kakeru, Banri, Iori!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.700
What do you think, Kiriyama?

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:43.040
It's hard to judge. It was highly entertaining.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:47.250
They have the ability to perform
difficult elements, but...

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:50.580
Unexpected, or rather, they've
taken advantage of the scoring.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.500
Interesting.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.500
Huh?

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.040
Wow, they really did it.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:59.450
But what's going to happen. Was that allowed?

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:02.700
It didn't go against any rules.
The fault is in how they're written.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:06.870
That Kuonji, he pretended
to compete against Himekawa,

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:10.700
but he was only focused on
showing off his team's performance.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:14.200
Did he involve Kogahara just to stir things up?

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.370
But...

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:21.450
The performance by Kuonji's team gripped
the audience's heart, without a doubt.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:26.660
They got a high entertainment score
and achieved an unrivaled score.

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:30.000
But because of their occasional mistakes...

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.750
...they couldn't beat Himekawa's team.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:41.540
"2. Kusano Mukaibara High School
3. Yokohama Super Global High School"

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.660
"2. Kusano Mukaibara High School
3. Yokohama Super Global High School"

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.660
--We did it!
--All right!

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.200
"2. Kusano Mukaibara High School
3. Yokohama Super Global High School"

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.200
Great job, Himekawa!

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.700
"Schools Qualifying for Grand Prix Finals"

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.700
"St. Clavis Gakuin High School
Chutei University Kamimaezu High School"

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.200
"Eimei Academy High School
Ionodai High School
Matsuyama Fukuonji High School
Kogahara High School"

00:20:57.080 --> 00:21:03.290
You ended up taking third, but your free skate
performance was truly phenomenal.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:05.080
It was my favorite.

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:09.120
Thank you very much. I'd be lying
if I said I have no regrets,

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:13.660
but I'm proud that I've brought a new way
of performing to skate-leading.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.450
"Skate-leading Path of the Challenger"

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.450
We're already preparing for next year,
so please cheer us on.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:17.700
We're already preparing for next year,
so please cheer us on.

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:18.660
Look forward to it!

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:19.700
We'll do it!

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.000
To your hearts--

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:24.290
--Mi*Leon!
--Noa!

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.120
He's on TV again.

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:30.410
The show needs to wrap things up.
In any case, it's the end for this segment.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:32.830
But the season isn't over yet, right?

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:33.700
That's right.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:39.370
And Kuonji will now be commentating
for the Grand Prix finals!

00:21:39.370 --> 00:21:40.410
I'll do my best.

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:41.450
What?!

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:44.580
Do you think he lost on purpose to do that?

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:47.750
No way. He would've done
both commentating and skating--

00:21:47.750 --> 00:21:50.370
Live broadcaster, commentator, and athlete.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.080
I thought I would do all three at once.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:54.830
Don't you think it would've
been cooler that way?

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.580
Maeshima, you were right.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:59.700
Could you really be joining his team next year?

00:21:59.700 --> 00:22:02.290
Yeah, right.

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:05.450
Nobody knows what lies in the future!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.250
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:40.330
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:40.330
Hey, Shinozaki, the one
who shares my princely title--

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:41.830
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:41.830
--You're--
--I have a proposal.

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:43.660
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:43.660
Wanna hold a birthday event together?

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:45.000
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:45.000
--If I recall--
--I know.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.160
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.160
We'll get ten more people
and celebrate every month.

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:49.290
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:49.290
--The waffle--
--We're really on the same wavelength.

00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:50.910
"Next time" "Final"

00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:50.910
--Yeah.
--Yup!
